  "description": "Impute NaN values in a dataset using column-wise summary statistics (mean, median, or mode) while preserving observed entries.\n\nImputation prevents sample deletion, preserving statistical power in downstream models.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\n\\hat{x}_{ij} = \\begin{cases} x_{ij} & x_{ij} \\neq \\text{NaN} \\\\ \\operatorname{stat}(\\mathbf{x}_{:, j}) & x_{ij} = \\text{NaN} \\end{cases}\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Identify NaN elements across each feature column\n2. Calculate specified aggregation statistic on valid observations\n3. Replace NaN entries with the column imputation value\n\n### Returns\nNested list with missing values imputed.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Missing Value Imputation\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nIn computational mathematics and machine learning, robust algorithmic routines ensure calculations are both mathematically sound and computationally efficient. **Missing Value Imputation** implements a core computational building block.\n\nImputation prevents sample deletion, preserving statistical power in downstream models. In this problem, the goal is to: impute nan values in a dataset using column-wise summary statistics (mean, median, or mode) while preserving observed entries.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\n\\hat{x}_{ij} = \\begin{cases} x_{ij} & x_{ij} \\neq \\text{NaN} \\\\ \\operatorname{stat}(\\mathbf{x}_{:, j}) & x_{ij} = \\text{NaN} \\end{cases}\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Identify NaN elements across each feature column\n2. **Phase 2**: Calculate specified aggregation statistic on valid observations\n3. **Phase 3**: Replace NaN entries with the column imputation value\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Algorithmic Complexity**: Designing routines with optimal time and space complexity ensures they scale gracefully to large datasets.\n* **Numerical Accuracy**: Safeguarding calculations against floating-point underflow or division by zero ensures consistent results.\n* **Vectorization**: Implementing operations with contiguous array buffers avoids interpreter overhead.",
  "examples": [
    "Input: matrix = [[1.0, NaN], [3.0, 4.0], [5.0, 6.0]], strategy = \"mean\"\n\nOutput: [[1.0, 5.0], [3.0, 4.0], [5.0, 6.0]]\n\nExplanation: Evaluated ml_imputation under standard test conditions."
